# Senior Fullstack Next.js & TypeScript Engineering Standards
# Target: Cursor (.cursorrules) / Claude Code (CLAUDE.md) / Antigravity (AGENTS.md)
# Framework: Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Shadcn UI

## 1. Architecture & Code Organization
- Always use Next.js App Router (`app/` directory).
- Separate Client and Server Components strictly:
  - Keep components Server Components by default.
  - Add `'use client'` only when using hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`), browser APIs, or interactivity.
- Colocate styles, tests, and types near the components when modular.
- Use kebab-case for directories and file names (e.g., `user-profile-card.tsx`).

## 2. TypeScript & Type Safety
- Strict type checking enabled at all times. Never use `any`.
- Define explicit interfaces/types for all Component Props, Server Action payloads, and API responses.
- Use Zod schemas for runtime validation of all user inputs, environment variables, and external API responses.

## 3. Server Actions & Mutations
- All data mutations must go through Next.js Server Actions with `'use server'`.
- Validate inputs inside Server Actions using Zod before any database or service call.
- Always return consistent response schemas: `{ success: boolean, data?: T, error?: string }`.
- Call `revalidatePath` or `revalidateTag` immediately after data mutations to keep the UI in sync.

## 4. UI/UX & Tailwind Standards
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes; avoid inline styles and raw CSS files unless custom animations require it.
- Ensure dark mode support using `dark:` variants with semantic variables.
- Maintain accessible markup: proper ARIA labels, semantic HTML tags (`<header>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<nav>`), keyboard navigation.
- Implement responsive design mobile-first (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`).

## 5. Error Handling & Guardrails
- Implement `error.tsx` and `loading.tsx` for every route segment.
- Log server-side errors with structured metadata.
- Never expose sensitive environment variables (`NEXT_PUBLIC_` only for public client keys).
